Chris Palomares - cssc3146 --> Please use this account for grading.
Eduardo Valdovinos - cssc3166

Project Description:
This program create seven chatbot threads. Each thread writes a quote to a shared file named QUOTE.txt. 
A POSIX semaphore named FLAG is used so that only one thread can write to the file at a time. This prevents the file contents from becoming corrupted.

Files:
bots.cpp	- Main source file containing the thread and semaphore logic
Makefile	- Builds the executable named bots
README		- Project information and instructions

How to Compile:
make

How to Run:
./bots

How to Clean:
make clean

Program Behavior:
When the program starts, it creates QUOTE.txt and writes the process ID.
Then it creates seven threads. Even numbered threads write the Brian
Kernighan quote every 2 seconds. Odd numbered threads write the Edsger
Dijkstra quote every 3 seconds. Each thread writes to the file 8 total times.
The semaphore FLAG protects the shared file during each write.

Testing:
The program was compiled and tested on edoras using g++ and pthreads.
After running, QUOTE.txt contained the process ID followed by the thread quote 
entries.

Design Decisions:

- We used a POSIX semaphore FLAG to ensure only 1 thread can write to the shared file (QUOTE.txt) at a time.
- We used a thread IDs to determine which quote is written to the shared file.

Lessons Learned:

We learned how to create and synchronize POSIX threads.
We also learned how to use semaphores to ensure that the shared file 
is written to one at a time to avoid a mixed up file output.

No known bugs at this time.
